WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
Most people think starting a business

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.560
requires tens of thousands of dollars

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.480
and a business degree and some kind of

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:09.360
special skill. But I'm going to show you

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:11.600
nine businesses you could literally

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.440
start this week for less than a thousand

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.000
dollars. And some of them are making

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.640
people six figures a year doing work

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.520
that most people aren't even thinking

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:21.160
about. So my name's Austin Zaback and

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.480
I've been building businesses for over a

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.320
decade in the real estate industry, pest

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.840
control, and a bunch of other stuff. And

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.880
so if at any point in the video you get

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.240
any value, do me a huge favor, go ahead

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.680
and smash that like button and it'll

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.000
help get this video in front of more

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.680
people who need to see it. All right, so

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.480
let's start with the most unglamorous

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.200
one on the list and probably the one

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.800
that's going to make you say there's no

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.680
way. And that is dog poop cleaning. Now

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.480
this industry is bigger than most people

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:48.240
realize and is actually growing really

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:50.440
fast. In 2024 alone, 66% of US

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:53.400
households reported owning at least one

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:55.560
pet. That's 86.9 million homes. And out

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.880
of those, 65 million of them own at

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.080
least one dog, making dogs the most

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:02.280
popular pet in the country. And those

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:05.320
dogs produce over 10 million tons of

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:07.880
waste every single year, over 20 billion

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:09.840
pounds. A single dog drops about three

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.760
quarters of a pound a day and most of it

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.320
goes uncollected. And the people who own

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.960
those dogs, well, they love their

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.640
animals just like I do, but they don't

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.960
want to deal with that, right? And that

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:20.840
is your business. The pet waste removal

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.960
market is already in the hundreds of

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:26.920
millions and it's projected to hit 537

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:30.000
million dollars by 2035, growing on an

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.240
average of 7.2% a year, which is a trend

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.800
line that you want to be on the right

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:34.760
side of. Now let me make this real for

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.960
you with an actual example because I've

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:39.800
actually seen it first hand. So I had a

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:42.040
poop scooper who I found online. Now she

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:44.280
built a route of 300 customers and she

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:46.200
was coming to my house one time per

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.800
week. And in about 10 minutes she would

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.040
come into my backyard, clean up all of

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.600
the waste, sanitize all my turf, and she

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.840
was out of there. One day I walked out

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:54.680
and I started talking to her and I was

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:57.160
asking her how many jobs she could do in

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:58.400
a day and she was doing 30 jobs a day

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:01.000
and she actually had quite a few

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:03.720
employees and each employee was doing 30

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:06.320
a day. At an average of $69 a month per

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:08.119
customer, she was doing about $20,000 a

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:09.880
month, which is just over a quarter of a

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:11.640
million dollars a year picking up dog

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:14.480
poop. And the startup cost to get into

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:16.560
this is literally a rake, a scoop, some

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.840
bins, maybe to store your waste,

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.640
disinfectant bags, gloves, and a

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.440
reliable car with a little bit of

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.120
storage to haul it all out of there. So

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:26.560
all in, you're looking at probably about

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.560
$500 to get started. And there is almost

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:30.800
no business on earth with that kind of

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.520
return on that kind of upfront

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:34.000
investment. And the real power here, if

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:36.200
you know anything about it, is the

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.760
recurring revenue model. These aren't

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:40.840
just one-time jobs. Customers pay you

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:43.080
every single month recurring. You're

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:45.360
going to the same yard, the same route,

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:47.160
and it runs like clockwork. You build

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:49.080
your route tight, optimize it by the

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:51.280
neighborhood, and you either scale by

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:53.640
adding more scoopers like she did, or

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.800
you run a lean solo operation and you

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:57.840
clear some serious cash. Is it

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:00.400
unglamorous? Of course it is, but it's

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:02.600
recurring and it is scalable. The jobs

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.400
that nobody wants are almost always the

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:06.320
jobs that are worth doing. The second

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:08.120
one has become super popular and that is

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:09.520
power washing. And what if I told you

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.120
that you could take a thousand dollar

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.160
investment and build a business that

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.080
does over a hundred grand a month? That

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:17.120
is exactly what happened with a guy that

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:18.760
I know personally. Before starting his

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.880
pressure washer business, he was a

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:22.760
financial advisor and he heard how

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.080
consistent the demand was in pressure

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.880
washing. He made the jump and on day one

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:29.240
he bought a trailer, he bought a water

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:31.200
tank, a hose, and a surface cleaner. He

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:33.360
didn't have any experience, he didn't

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:35.280
have any industry background, he just

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.880
watched some YouTube videos online like

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.800
the one you're watching right now. He

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:40.960
showed up and he got to work. And four

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.920
years in, his best month crossed over a

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:44.520
hundred grand. And that is the kind of

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:46.440
story that should make you put down

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:48.320
whatever excuse you've been holding on

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:50.040
to. So let's talk about why it works.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:52.880
The US pressure washing industry

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:55.680
generates over 1.2 billion dollars in

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:57.960
revenue across more than 32,000

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:59.960
companies and it is still growing.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:02.280
Residential and commercial demand is

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:04.200
consistent year-round. People always

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:05.960
need their driveways, their patios,

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:08.320
their storefronts, and their building

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:09.920
exteriors cleaned. It's not seasonal the

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:12.000
way that some people think. It is a

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.360
service with near infinite repeat

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.480
customers because all things get dirty

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:18.640
again all the time. Average residential

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:20.640
jobs run anywhere from $400 to a

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:22.600
thousand bucks just to wash a home's

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:24.360
exterior. And the best part is that you

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:26.520
can launch this business for around a

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:28.600
thousand dollars covering your equipment

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:30.760
and even picking up used gear to keep

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:32.880
costs down. With a pressure washer, a

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:35.600
surface cleaner, some hoses, and some

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:38.040
basic marketing, you can be running jobs

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:39.880
within a week after you decide to start.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.560
And there is another angle and that is

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:43.120
potentially looking at trash can

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:45.040
cleaning. So think about this. You're

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:46.920
already at the house, you already have

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.840
the equipment, the water and the

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:51.320
cleaning solution. The customer's trash

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.880
cans are literally sitting right there.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:54.560
You can go knock on their door or text

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:56.400
them and give them a call and you can

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:59.160
offer to clean them for an extra 20 to

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:01.280
30 dollars per can and most homeowners

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:03.800
will just say yes without even blinking.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:05.880
So that's a 40 to 60 dollar upsell on a

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:08.120
job that you were already doing. Now you

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:09.720
multiply that across every residential

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:11.640
customer on your route and you just

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:14.080
potentially added thousands of dollars a

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:15.880
month in revenue without adding extra

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.800
driving and miles and wear and tear in

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:19.080
your vehicles. You're monetizing what is

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:20.840
already right in front of you and that

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:22.600
is my favorite thing in the world to do.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:24.160
And the best operators in this space

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:26.120
don't just pressure wash, they become

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:28.240
the full exterior maintenance solution

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:30.120
for their customers. And that is how you

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:32.520
increase your average ticket and

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:34.400
recurring revenue and make yourself hard

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:35.880
to replace. Before I get into the third

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:38.000
point, I want to say something that I

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:40.800
truly believe. You will never be rich

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:42.400
until you stop underestimating how lazy

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:44.600
people actually are. Because the

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:47.160
businesses that make the most consistent

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:49.240
money are almost always built around the

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:51.640
things that people simply don't want to

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:53.440
do and taking out trash is one of them.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:55.120
I actually did a full business tour with

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:57.760
the founder of a company called Can

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:00.160
Monkey, which is a company that does one

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:02.240
singular thing. They literally take out

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:05.040
your trash cans from your garage or your

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:07.080
backyard to the curb on collection day

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:09.720
and then they bring them back. That is

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:11.760
the entire service. And the idea started

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:13.400
with one simple observation. The founder

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:14.960
is walking his dog one night when he

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.880
watched his neighbor pull up in his

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:18.800
Mercedes, drive straight into the

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:20.520
garage, and leave the trash can at the

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:22.160
end of the driveway. He thought, if I

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:24.080
don't want to do this, neither does my

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:26.680
neighbor. And that one observation

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:28.400
turned into a very profitable business.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:30.440
And that same founder told me that they

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:33.800
had over 4,000

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:36.360
active subscriptions across 18 states

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:38.240
with over 500 runners taking out and

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:40.760
doing those routes. And they charge

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:43.160
$49.99 a month per property and that

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:45.840
covers trash and recycling going out and

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:48.680
coming back every single week. At 4,000

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:50.720
active subscriptions, that is 200 grand

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:53.720
a month in recurring revenue from

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:55.720
literally rolling out people's trash can

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:58.760
to the curb. And the churn rate on their

00:06:55.720 --> 00:07:00.440
homeowner subscribers is less than 1%.

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:02.200
So once people have this service done

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:04.480
for them, they never go back to doing it

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:06.800
themselves. It's that same psychology as

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:09.000
the poop scooper business. Once somebody

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:11.320
does it for you and you enjoy the luxury

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:12.880
of not hassling, you literally forget

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:14.440
about the cost on your credit card

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:15.720
statement. Now think about this from a

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:17.840
startup perspective. You don't need a

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:19.680
truck, you don't need special equipment,

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:21.840
you literally need a neighborhood, a

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:23.440
schedule, and the discipline to show up

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:25.360
every week. Think about who actually

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:27.560
needs this service. We're talking

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:29.360
elderly residents who can't manage heavy

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:31.560
cans in hotter cold climates

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:33.040
potentially, people with second homes

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:35.480
who wanted to look like somebody's

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:37.480
living there for security reasons, and

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:39.800
busy families who don't just want to

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:41.240
deal with it. Also, Airbnb and

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:43.640
short-term rental properties where

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:45.600
somebody has to take the cans out in

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:47.480
between guests staying in their home.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:50.560
And every single one of those has a

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:52.040
problem and you are the solution. Okay,

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:54.160
the fourth business is one of my

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:56.560
favorites. People will always accumulate

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:58.560
stuff, right? They move, they renovate,

00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:00.200
okay? They downsize, they clean out

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:02.000
their garage that they haven't touched

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:03.400
in a decade. And when they're ready to

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.240
get rid of it, they don't want to deal

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:07.920
with it, okay? They want somebody to

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:09.800
show up, load it, and make it disappear.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:11.400
And that is junk removal. And the

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:13.400
opportunity here is actually pretty

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:15.840
massive. So the US waste collection

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:19.680
services industry is expected to surpass

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:21.400
90 billion in annual revenue by 2030. So

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:23.880
this isn't really a niche, it is a

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:26.240
massive recession resistant market with

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:29.120
room for small operators to carve out

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:30.880
serious income in their local area. For

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:33.520
a single junk removal vehicle, you can

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:35.760
realistically generate 500 to 1500

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:38.120
dollars a day. Jobs are priced typically

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:39.960
by volume, so you show up, you quote the

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:41.560
job on the spot, and then you load all

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:43.680
that stuff, and you get paid. There's

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:45.840
not really any invoicing or getting paid

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:47.120
30 days later, you get cash in hand as

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:49.200
soon as you're done with the job. And

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:51.720
the average cost of a junk removal job

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:53.720
is anywhere between 250 to 300 dollars

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:55.720
for a standard load. Now here's what I

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:57.880
love about this business from a startup

00:08:55.720 --> 00:09:00.320
standpoint. The barriers to entry are

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:02.960
really low. The startup costs are pretty

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:04.200
modest and the overhead is minimal. And

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:06.000
if you already have a truck, you're

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:07.520
halfway there. The real way to crush it

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:09.720
in junk removal is just through

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:12.320
relationships, okay? Think real estate

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:14.600
agents, property managers, estate sale

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:16.480
companies, contractors. These people

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:18.400
have a consistent stream of properties

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:20.320
that need to be cleared out. Landlords

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:22.120
and property managers alone rely heavily

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:23.960
on junk removal companies to clear out

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.600
units between tenants. And with the

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:29.000
average apartment turnover rate in the

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:31.080
US sitting around 40 to 50% annually,

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:32.720
that is a steady reliable pipeline of

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:34.960
work. And the best part of the business

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:36.920
is how simple the growth model is. You

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:38.760
start with one truck, maybe a trailer,

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:40.960
and yourself, and when you get busy

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:42.800
enough, you add another truck, you add

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:44.680
another driver, and you rinse and you

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:46.440
repeat. You don't need a complicated

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:48.680
strategy, you just need to outwork the

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:50.480
competition and market yourself and your

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:52.640
business in a way that your competition

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:53.960
is not. Number five is one that I do not

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:55.800
see a lot of people talking about and

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:57.840
that is solar panel cleaning. Most

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:59.360
people see solar panels and they think

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:01.040
clean energy, but what they don't think

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:03.680
about is who's actually cleaning those

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:06.160
panels and that is the opportunity.

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:08.160
Dirt, dust, pollen, and bird droppings

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:10.080
build up on solar panels over time and

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:12.120
they block the sunlight from reaching

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:13.800
the cells. That means that the system

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:15.960
that the homeowner paid tens of

